  "note": "Election of the Warrenpoint Urban Council, January 1929. Both wards were contested: five seats in West Ward and seven in East Ward. Brown and Russell tied for the fifth seat on 170 votes; lots were drawn and Brown was declared elected. The other five Unionist candidates were returned. 407 of 465 electors voted; 6 spoiled papers."
